  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="ea3930e1-5534-54c4-a446-18ce8a78100a" activityNameId="6b5059f3-0410-5cd8-9fde-39eec43edd6d" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Asphalt concrete (AC) base layer, 30% recycling, high temperature, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Asphalt concrete (AC) base layer, 30% recycling, high temperature, at plant
Modern Swiss technologies for regional storage facilities, material extraction, and asphalt production. Based on survey data from 73 asphalt mixing plants. 
UUID: ad2d0051-6556-4a86-a65d-853179580a25
This dataset covers the production of average Asphalt Concrete (AC T) base layers in Switzerland, with 30% reclaimed asphalt. The process represents an average AC T, derived from the mean material composition of multiple AC T S, AC T N, AC T L and AC T H layers. It includes raw material extraction, transportation, and manufacturing processes.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: Production of hot mix asphalt concrete AC T, using industrial machinery.
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 351352456 t 
Sampling: Survey
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_ad2d0051-6556-4a86-a65d-853179580a25.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
